    73	## 2. Exact attachment lemmas
    74	
    75	**Cycle lemma.** Let `T` have connected tree resolution graph and let `Q` be
    76	an irreducible reduced curve not contained in `T`. If the normalization of
    77	`Q` has two distinct branches over `T`, then every embedded resolution of
    78	`T union Q` has a cycle in its dual multigraph. Extra blowups either attach a
    79	pendant vertex or subdivide an edge of the resolved `T` tree. The single
    80	strict-transform vertex of `Q` then has two edges into that tree; distinct
    81	endpoints close the unique path, while equal endpoints form a parallel-edge
    82	cycle. The statement covers two physical points, two analytic branches over
    83	one point, singular `Q`, tangencies, and attachments deep in exceptional
    84	trees.
    85	
    86	**Exact boundary critical set.** In a local chart
    87	
    88	```text
    89	X: f(u,v,z)=0,                 H: f(0,v,z)=0,
    90	```
    91	
    92	the critical divisor of `pi` is `f_z|X=0`. A point of `H` lies on it exactly
    93	when it is a singular point of `H_red` or a smooth point where the relevant
    94	branch is critical for projection `H->L_infinity`; equivalently the vertical
    95	line has intersection multiplicity at least two there.
    96	
    97	This Cartier critical divisor has no component contained in `H`. Indeed, if
    98	a reduced factor `h` of `f(0,v,z)` also divides `f_z(0,v,z)`, coprimality with
    99	the residual factor forces `h|h_z`, hence in characteristic zero `h_z=0`.
   100	Then `h=h(v)` defines the excluded vertical `(1,0)` component. Purity of the
   101	Cartier divisor therefore puts every boundary critical point in `Rbar` and
   102	shows that there is no additional, unclassified attachment kind.
   103	
   104	**Nonemptiness.** `R_red` is nonempty. A positive-dimensional fibre away
   105	from `H`, if present, lies in the critical locus. If no such fibre exists,
   106	properness makes `pi` finite; an everywhere-etale degree-three map from the
   107	irreducible `X` to the simply connected `P2` is impossible. Since the
   108	critical divisor has no component in `H`, its affine part is nonempty.
   109	
   110	## 3. Attachment dichotomy
   111	
   112	For a rational component's normalization of degree `b` over the infinity
   113	line, Riemann--Hurwitz gives total ramification `2b-2`, with contribution at
   114	most `b-1` at one point. Thus every degree-three component and every
   115	degree-two component has at least two distinct normalization critical points.
   116	The forest budget prevents their images from identifying in the relevant
   117	`F1,F2,F4` configurations. In `F7`, the two length-two contacts with its two
   118	disjoint sections are distinct double-root points. Therefore:
   119	
   120	```text
   121	F1, F2, F4, F7 + irreducible R_red
   122	    => two branches of Rbar over H
   123	    => cycle in the resolved full boundary
   124	    => contradiction.                                 (3.1)
   125	```
   126	
   127	In `F5`, every component has projection degree one. The exact boundary
   128	critical set is only its unique triple/contact point `p_0`, so the attachment
   129	argument supplies only one branch and does not eliminate the type. The
   130	ramification Cartier class is
   131	
   132	```text
   133	R_pi=(2A+B)|X,                 H.R_pi=8,
   134	```
   135	
   136	and all eight intersection units are concentrated at `p_0`.
   137	
   138	Combining the cases gives the promoted conclusion:
   139	
   140	> In the declared smooth, reduced, projectively finite quadratic block
   141	> scope, every survivor has reducible `R_red` or infinity type `F5`. If
   142	> `R_red` is irreducible, the only surviving infinity type is `F5`, with its
   143	> entire boundary ramification intersection concentrated at the unique
   144	> triple point.
   145	
   146	This is a necessary-condition dichotomy. It proves neither that `F5` occurs
   147	nor that reducible ramification is compatible with a first leg.
